  "credit": "\u00a9 NASA / Ames Research Center \u2014 U.S. Government work, public domain. First spacecraft to fly past Saturn (1979-09-01) and the first to image the planet at close range. Used Jupiter's gravity to reach Saturn, demonstrating the gravity-assist technique that would later send Voyager 2 to Uranus and Neptune. Discovered Saturn's F ring + an additional small moon (Epimetheus). Carries the same Pioneer plaque as Pioneer 10. Signal lost 1995-09-30 from a heliocentric distance of ~43 AU; spacecraft heading toward the constellation Aquila.",
